// OPTIONAL — but recommended if you'll commit a fork.
//
// Copy this file to `Local.xcconfig` (same folder — git-ignored) and fill in the
// values below. Everything here is personal to you and must stay out of git.
//
// Without this file you can still set both values in Xcode (target → Signing &
// Capabilities). The catch is that Xcode then writes them into project.pbxproj,
// which IS tracked — so your Team ID and bundle id show up as an uncommitted diff
// forever, and are easy to commit by accident.

// ── Bundle identifier ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Apple requires this to be unique to you, so the committed default
// (com.example.DeckCheck) won't sign. Use reverse-DNS with your own name:
DECKCHECK_BUNDLE_ID = com.yourname.deckcheck

// NOTE: your Google OAuth client is tied to this value. If you change it after
// setting up OAuth, create a new iOS client for the new bundle id — see
// docs/setup/google-oauth-client.md.

// ── Apple Developer Team ID ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
// You must still pick your Team in Xcode once (Signing & Capabilities →
// Automatically manage signing) so it can provision your device — a free Apple ID
// works, no paid account needed. Setting it here as well is what keeps Xcode from
// writing it into project.pbxproj.
//
// To find your 10-character Team ID, run in Terminal:
//     security find-identity -v -p codesigning
// It's the code in parentheses after your name on an "Apple Development" identity.
// (Paid accounts can also read it at developer.apple.com → Membership.)
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID
